import lib/cadkernel/polyline_approximation3.dl

function check approximation3 {boolean:condition}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 94)

function approximation3 distance of {cad vector3:point} to {a pointer to a list:points}:
    execute:
        set best to @intrinsic("divide", 1.0, 0.0)
        loop index from 0 to ((the length of points) - 1):
            set start to the item at index in points
            set end to the item at (index + 1) in points
            set delta to the cad difference of end and start
            set squared to the cad squared length of delta
            set parameter to 0.0
            if squared > 0.0:
                set parameter to (the cad dot of (the cad difference of point and start) and delta) / squared
            clamp parameter between 0.0 and 1.0
            set nearest to the cad sum of start and (delta scaled by parameter)
            set best to the minimum of best and (the cad distance from point to nearest)
        return best

set controls to a list containing the cad zero vector3
append (a cad vector3 with x 1.0, y 3.0 and z 1.0) to controls
append (a cad vector3 with x 2.0, y -1.0 and z 2.0) to controls
append (a cad vector3 with x 4.0, y 0.0 and z 3.0) to controls
set knots to a list containing 0.0
append 0.0 to knots
append 0.0 to knots
append 0.4 to knots
append 1.0 to knots
append 1.0 to knots
append 1.0 to knots
set weights to a list containing 1.0
append 3.0 to weights
append 0.5 to weights
append 2.0 to weights
set curve to the strict cad nurbs curve3 of degree 2 with controls controls, knots knots and weights weights
check approximation3 curve's valid
set coarse to the cad spline polyline of curve's value at precision 0
set fine to the cad spline polyline of curve's value at precision 20
check approximation3 (coarse's valid and fine's valid)
check approximation3 (fine's tolerance < coarse's tolerance)
check approximation3 ((the length of fine's points) >= (the length of coarse's points))
set first to the item at 0 in (fine's points)
set last to the last item of (fine's points)
set start to the cad point on curve's value at 0.0
set end to the cad point on curve's value at 1.0
check approximation3 (((first's x = start's x) and (first's y = start's y)) and (first's z = start's z))
check approximation3 (((last's x = end's x) and (last's y = end's y)) and (last's z = end's z))
loop step from 0 through 512:
    set point to the cad point on curve's value at ((step as a 64 bit floating-point number) / 512.0)
    check approximation3 ((approximation3 distance of point to (fine's points)) <= (fine's tolerance + 1e-10))
print "precision_is_monotonic_and_bounds_the_sampled_curve" as a line

clear controls
append the cad zero vector3 to controls
append (a cad vector3 with x 1.0, y 2.0 and z 0.0) to controls
append (a cad vector3 with x 2.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0) to controls
append (a cad vector3 with x 3.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0) to controls
clear weights
loop index from 0 to 4:
    append 1.0 to weights
set curve to the strict cad nurbs curve3 of degree 2 with controls controls, knots knots and weights weights
check approximation3 curve's valid
set result to the cad spline polyline of curve's value at precision 10
check approximation3 result's valid
set boundary to the cad point on curve's value at knot 0.4
set found to false
loop index from 0 to the length of result's points:
    if (the cad distance from (the item at index in (result's points)) to boundary) < 1e-12:
        set found to true
check approximation3 found
set refused to the cad spline polyline of curve's value at precision 100
check approximation3 (refused's valid = false)
clear controls
clear weights
set coordinates to [0.0,1.0,2.0,4.0,5.0,6.0]
loop index from 0 to 6:
    set value to the item at index in coordinates
    append (a cad vector3 with x value, y value and z value) to controls
    append 1.0 to weights
clear knots
loop index from 0 to 3:
    append 0.0 to knots
loop index from 0 to 3:
    append 0.5 to knots
loop index from 0 to 3:
    append 1.0 to knots
set curve to the strict cad nurbs curve3 of degree 2 with controls controls, knots knots and weights weights
check approximation3 curve's valid
set refused to the cad spline polyline of curve's value at precision 10
check approximation3 (refused's valid = false)
free controls
free knots
free weights
print "knot_boundaries_survive_and_discontinuous_curves_are_rejected" as a line
